{"action_id":"action.a49cc91af135440590d1dba9857f1a2f","result":{"provenance":{"allowance_slot":27,"cli_version":"codex-cli 0.153.4","configuration":"ignore-user-config; read-only; tools-disabled; no-resume","events_jsonl":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0ccf3-708d-7b03-9bf1-8e7508c106c1\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"coverage\\\": [\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"States the extended parallel run and mandatory transition date.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Background heading; no independent obligation.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u2\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies launch dates, submission context and the unavailable earlier circular.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u3\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Existing-channel acceptance attaches to the parallel run period.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Heading connects the extension with planned enhancements.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u5\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Monitoring and industry feedback explain enhancements without conditioning the submission duty.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u6\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Extends the parallel run to a fixed date; enhancement purpose does not establish a completion condition.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u8\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Distinguishes mandatory submission routing, announced reporting integration and optional fee-payment functionality.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Heading locates the practicability language within feedback and enquiries.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u10\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Practicability qualifies SFC review and enhancement; case-officer contact does not expressly confer a waiver.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies issuing division.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u12\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies issuing regulator.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"End marker; no substantive requirement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Supplies product categories relevant to covered-submission classification.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Expands WINGS; does not change route obligations or exceptions.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The selected control concerns individual applications and submissions to IPD about products it administers. It does not impose duties on every industry participant merely because the circular addresses the industry.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Footnote 1 identifies product categories, but classification of borderline products and communications remains unresolved. Footnote 2 expands WINGS without adding substantive conditions.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Existing-channel acceptance is temporally limited by the extended parallel run. Neither the enhancement rationale nor 'where practicable' supports an exception to the post-transition submission duty. The latter qualifies SFC review and enhancement, although its distribution between those two activities need not be resolved for this control.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u5\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"'Must' governs submission routing; 'will' announces extension and integration; 'can also' offers fee-payment functionality. The invitation to contact case officers is not express permission to bypass e-IP.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The original 29 October endpoint is extended through 29 November 2024, followed by mandatory routing from 30 November 2024. Launch and earlier-circular dates are historical context. No supplied wording makes commencement contingent on completion of enhancements.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The earlier circular and external-authorities.24ec50 are unavailable. Their possible scope qualifications cannot be supplied by inference. Both comparison diagnostics report incomparable fact bindings and provide no snapshots, so they establish no substantive counterexample.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does the unavailable 8 July 2024 circular specify contingencies, alternative channels or treatment of pending matters that qualify this control?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is footnote 1 exhaustive, and which borderline communications count as applications or submissions to IPD?\\\",\\n    \\\"Can aligned fact bindings and concrete snapshots be supplied for the two incomparable node pairs?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run preserves its existing-channel acceptance feature through 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n        \\\"The transition applies to the date of each submission event; no grandfathering rule for existing matters is supplied.\\\",\\n        \\\"Product and communication classifications must be established separately, with unknown facts remaining unknown.\\\",\\n        \\\"This proposal is limited to the retained text; unavailable authorities have not been treated as establishing or excluding additional exceptions.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"If you have any questions, please contact the relevant case officers.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Exception-attachment investigation retains the parent's event-based control. A proposed practicability exception for submitters fails because the qualification belongs to a separate sentence about SFC operations. A proposed delay until enhancements are complete also fails: their facilitation explains the fixed extension without making completion a condition. Optional annual-fee functionality supplies no exception for otherwise covered submissions. No materially different rival route rule is supported by the retained text. The strongest uncertainty is whether the missing earlier circular supplies additional qualifications; the incomparable diagnostics cannot resolve it.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The evaluated event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD. Classification must account for footnote 1; optional fee payment alone does not establish this fact.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_covered_submission\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean classification of one submission event\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date on which the evaluated application or submission is made to IPD.\\\",\\\"na